    "body": "## P1 authorization/privacy hardening\n\nStripe original-method refund paths loaded private financial records globally and only then compared ownership. That made a foreign existing PaymentIntent or refund id distinguishable from a missing one (`403` versus neutral `404`) and let another user's financial row cross the authorization boundary before ownership was established.\n\n## Change\n\n- lock the original `PaymentTransaction` through an owner-scoped `paymentIntentId + userId` query;\n- read refund state through an owner-scoped `refundRequestId + userId` query;\n- return the same neutral not-found contract for foreign and missing resources;\n- remove post-load ownership branches while preserving refund idempotency, currency/purpose checks, dispute guards, wallet reservation, provider dispatch and settlement behavior;\n- document the financial-resource privacy invariant.\n\n## Regression coverage\n\n- an outsider cannot enumerate a settled PaymentIntent through refund creation and reaches no dispute or wallet side effect;\n- an outsider cannot enumerate an existing refund status and never falls back to global `findById`;\n- the owner still reads refund state through the scoped lookup;\n- existing Stripe dispute/refund service coverage is updated for the scoped lock.\n\n## Roadmap\n\nAdvances the active endpoint-by-endpoint authorization, historical-resource privacy and IDOR audit (#615, #618, #620; umbrella #957).\n\n## Merge gate\n\nBranch is based on `master` `bfec9983850a052ca209a4b36881bba3ffe9a8d4`. Merge only after every relevant workflow is green on the exact current PR head, review threads are clear, and `master` is revalidated immediately before merge. If `master` moves, integrate it safely and rerun the exact-head gate. Merge commit only.",
